---
const title = 'Ephemeral — an interface for right now';
const description = 'A study of temporary, intent-led interfaces. Explore one social feed as a morning briefing, a focused conversation, or an evening collection. Entirely scripted.';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="light" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://shupp.dev/design/ephemeral/" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://shupp.dev/design/ephemeral/" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="preload" href="/ephemeral/fonts/martel-regular.woff" as="font" type="font/woff" crossorigin />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/ephemeral/ephemeral.css" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#experience">Skip to the interactive study</a>
    <header class="site-header wrap">
      <a class="wordmark" href="#">ephemeral<span aria-hidden="true">.</span></a>
      <nav aria-label="Page"><a href="#idea">The idea</a><a href="#experience">Try a day</a><a href="/portfolio">shupp.dev ↗</a></nav>
    </header>
    <main>
      <section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">An exploration in interface design · 01</p>
        <h1 id="hero-title">An interface<br />for <em>right now.</em></h1>
        <div class="hero-bottom">
          <a class="text-link" href="#experience">Spend a day with it <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
          <p>You open the same app.<br />You’re not always there for the same thing.<br /><strong>What if the interface could meet you there?</strong></p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="premise wrap" id="idea" aria-labelledby="premise-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">01 / The reason</p>
        <div><h2 id="premise-title">A feed holds everything.<br />A moment asks for something.</h2>
          <p>Sometimes you need to catch up. Sometimes you’re following one question. Sometimes you just want to wander. Ephemeral gives that visit a useful shape, then lets the shape go.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="study wrap" id="experience" aria-labelledby="study-title">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div><p class="eyebrow">02 / One app. Three visits.</p><h2 id="study-title">Same people.<br />A different reason to open.</h2></div>
          <p>A fictional social app, <em>Commonplace</em>.<br />Compare its regular feed with a view shaped by your need. Both use the same posts available at that time.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="day-picker" role="group" aria-label="Sample visit">
          <button type="button" data-visit="morning" aria-pressed="true"><span>01</span><strong>Morning</strong><span>08:00</span></button>
          <button type="button" data-visit="afternoon" aria-pressed="false"><span>02</span><strong>Afternoon</strong><span>13:00</span></button>
          <button type="button" data-visit="evening" aria-pressed="false"><span>03</span><strong>Evening</strong><span>20:30</span></button>
        </div>
        <div class="visit-context"><p id="visit-context">You have a few minutes before your day begins.</p><p id="snapshot-label">6 sample posts available</p></div>
        <div class="comparison" role="group" aria-label="Interface to compare">
          <button type="button" data-mode="feed" aria-pressed="false">Regular feed <span>Control</span></button>
          <button type="button" data-mode="ephemeral" aria-pressed="true">Ephemeral <span>Responds to intent</span></button>
        </div>

        <div class="app" id="commonplace">
          <header class="app-header"><span class="app-name">commonplace</span><div class="app-actions"><button type="button" id="saved-toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="saved-panel">Saved <span id="saved-count">0</span></button><button type="button" id="preferences-toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="preferences-panel">Preferences</button></div></header>
          <div id="preferences-panel" class="preferences" hidden>
            <p class="eyebrow">Your preferences for this visit</p>
            <label><input id="design-only" type="checkbox" /> Only design &amp; tools</label>
            <label><input id="short-brief" type="checkbox" checked /> Keep my brief short</label>
            <label><input id="reading-first" type="checkbox" /> Put longer reads first when browsing</label>
            <p>Preferences stay as the view changes. This sketch doesn’t track your browsing.</p>
          </div>
          <section id="saved-panel" class="saved-panel" aria-labelledby="saved-heading" hidden><h3 id="saved-heading">Kept for later</h3><div id="saved-content"></div></section>
          <div class="intent-area" id="intent-area">
            <form id="intent-form">
              <label class="eyebrow" for="intent-query">What are you here for?</label>
              <div class="query-line"><input id="intent-query" type="text" value="Catch me up. I have three minutes." maxlength="180" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="query-help" /><button type="submit" aria-label="Apply your intent">Go <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button></div>
            </form>
            <div class="intent-choices" role="group" aria-label="Try an intent at any time">
              <button type="button" data-intent="brief" aria-pressed="true">Catch me up</button><button type="button" data-intent="focus" aria-pressed="false">Understand Fold</button><button type="button" data-intent="browse" aria-pressed="false">Let me browse</button>
            </div>
            <p id="query-help" class="query-help">Try these sample intents, or type one. Add “only design” or “longer reads.”</p>
          </div>
          <div id="scene" class="scene"></div>
          <p id="announcement" class="sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></p>
          <footer class="app-footer"><p id="format-note"></p><button type="button" id="why-toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="why-panel">Why this view?</button></footer>
          <div id="why-panel" class="why-panel" hidden></div>
          <noscript><p class="no-script">Enable JavaScript to explore the scripted examples. The design principles below are readable without it.</p></noscript>
        </div>
        <div class="study-note"><p id="benefit-note">The user can finish catching up without deciding where an endless feed ends.</p><span>Fictional posts · authored responses · no inference</span></div>
      </section>

      <section class="principles wrap" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">03 / What changes. What stays.</p>
        <h2 id="principles-title">Familiar at the edges.<br />Fluid in the middle.</h2>
        <div class="principle-grid">
          <article><span class="small-number">01</span><h3>Intent leads.</h3><p>The user’s request has the final say. A morning visit can be an evening kind of visit. Time offers context; it never decides the task.</p></article>
          <article><span class="small-number">02</span><h3>Habits suggest.</h3><p>With permission, repeated behavior could suggest “Your usual quick catch-up?” Let the person accept or change it. This study uses authored examples, not observed behavior.</p></article>
          <article><span class="small-number">03</span><h3>Keep the anchors.</h3><p>Navigation, preferences, original posts, and saved items remain reachable. Change the view when intent changes, while keeping controls where people expect them.</p></article>
          <article><span class="small-number">04</span><h3>Let a visit end.</h3><p>A catch-up can be complete. A temporary view can disappear. What someone deliberately saves should outlive that view.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="closing wrap" aria-labelledby="closing-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">The question to test</p>
        <h2 id="closing-title">Did you find what<br />you came for?</h2>
        <div class="closing-copy"><p>Compare the same task on the same posts. Look for less sorting, fewer detours, and a clearer sense of completion. Check whether people still understand what was included—and can find what was left out.</p><p>This is a hypothesis you can interact with. No model is running. Briefings, matches, and explanations are written in advance; every source post is available in the control.</p></div>
        <a class="text-link" href="#experience">Try another kind of visit ↑</a>
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer class="site-footer wrap"><a href="/portfolio">A design study by Erikk Shupp ↗</a><span>Black / white. Here / gone.</span><details><summary>Type &amp; credits</summary><p>Martel + Nunito Sans. Adapted from a pairing explored with <a href="https://fontjoy.com/">Fontjoy</a>. <a href="/ephemeral/fonts/LICENSES.txt">Font licenses</a>.</p></details></footer>
    <script is:inline type="module" src="/ephemeral/ephemeral.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>
